    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="22">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 22</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ sy [ælc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.4"/> getrywa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.5-2"/> man, þe tihtbysig] nære, ⁊ naðor ne burste ne að ne ordal, innan hundrede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.6-2"/> anfealdre lade wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ sy ælc getreowe man, ðe tihtbysi nǽre, ⁊ naðer ne burste ne að ne ordal, innan hundrede anfealde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.2"/> lade wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>And sy ælc getriwa man, þe tyhtbysig nare, ⁊ naðor ne burste ne að ne ordal, innan his hundrede ánfealdre lade wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Et sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.5"/> omnis homo credibilis, qui non fuerit accusationibus infamatus (<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.6"/>latrocinio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.7"/> occupatus), et neutrum ei fregerit uel iuramentum uel ordalium, in hundreto (aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.8"/> extra) simplici láda (purgatione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.9"/>) dignus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Si sit autem quisquam fidelis homo, qui iuste non fuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.5-3"/> calumniatus de aliqua turpi re, et cui iuramentum non fregerit in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.6-3"/> ore nec iudicium ferri uel aquę, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.7-2"/> Angli uocant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.8-2"/> (dicunt) þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe ue bærst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_22.lnote.oe.9-2"/> ne aþ ne ordel, iste talis, si aliquando calumniatus fuerit, purget se simplici purgatione.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Sitque omnis fidelis, qui calumpniosus non fuit, cuique nunquam defecit iuramentum uel Dei iudicium, in centenario simplici purgatione dignus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="22" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="184" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ sy ælc getreowe man ðe tihtbysi nǽre ⁊ naðer ne burste ne að ne ordal innan hundred<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IICn_22.robnote.fn.11"/>e anfealde lade wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="264" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And sy ælc getrywa man þe tihtbysig nære and naðor ne burste ne að ne ordal, innan hundrede anfealdre lade wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_22.lnote.de.1"/> jeder glaubwürdige Mann, [nämlich] der nicht bescholten gewesen, und dem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_22.lnote.de.2"/> weder Eid noch Ordal fehlgeschlagen ist, sei einfachen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_22.lnote.de.3"/> Reinigungsbeweises theilhaftig [mit Eideshelfern, die er selbst wählt] innerhalb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22.lnote.de.4"/> der (seiner <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) Hundertschaft.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22.lnote.de.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every trustworthy man who has not been of bad repute, and for whom neither oath nor ordeal has failed, be entitled to the single clearing [with oath-helpers of his own choosing] within the (his, A) hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="185" ed="#robertson"/>And every trustworthy man, who has never earned a bad reputation<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_22.robnote.n.1"/> and who has never failed<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_22.robnote.n.2"/> either in oath or in ordeal, shall be entitled to clear himself within the hundred<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_22.robnote.n.3"/> by the simple oath of exculpation<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22.robnote.n.4"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And every trustworthy man, who has not been frequently accused, and has failed neither at oath nor at ordeal, is to be entitled to the simple process of exculpation within his hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="265" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And every trustworthy man who had never been under suspicion and had not failed an oath or ordeal, shall be eligible to exonerate himself by the simple oath of exculpation.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="324"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-1">I Atr 1.1f.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. I Atr. 1, 1 f.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_14">Leis Wl 14</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1">I Atr 1–1.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 22: I Atr 1-1:2</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘[ælc getrywa man, þe tihtbysig]’ is on an erasure in the 16th century. Liebermann compares I Atr 1, 1 f.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 325, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">innan: innan his A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iu. de. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iu. de. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. I</hi> 5, 4 <hi rend="italic">Hs. A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. I 5, 4 MS A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o. h. c. sit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o. h. c. sit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">id est <hi rend="italic">fügt T zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">id est added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur DmT; fehlt übr., auch Hn.</hi> 64, 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only DmT; lacking in the others, also in Hn. 64, 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aut extra <hi rend="italic">nur Dm</hi> [<hi rend="italic">falsch</hi>]; <hi rend="italic">fehlt übr., auch Hn</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aut extra only Dm [wrong]; lacking in the others, also in Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur Hk, ohne</hi> lada; <hi rend="italic">fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only Hk, without lada; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ælc — bysig <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. auf Rasur G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ælc — bysig in the 16th cent. on an erasure G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man getriwa man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man getriwa man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">his hundred <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">his hundred Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">erit <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erit Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">more <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">more Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">que <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">que Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uo. <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> di. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uo. Cb; di. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">bert <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">bert Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die schon hier angeschnittene Stelle aus Atr wird <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 30 seitenlang ausgeschrieben.—Das Stück 22—23, ohne 22, 2, ist benutzt durch Hn 64, 9. Cnut folgt hier nicht dem III Atr 3, 1f., der nur Denalagu betrifft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The passage from Atr already touched on here is copied out at length, over several pages, <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 30.—The section 22—23, without 22, 2, is used by Hn 64, 9. Cnut does not follow III Atr 3, 1f. here, which concerns only the Danelaw</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">zu ergänzen aus vorigem <hi rend="italic">þe</hi>, das dort Nominativ, hier Dativ</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be supplied from the preceding <hi rend="italic">þe</hi>, which is nominative there and dative here</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eideshelfer 27c—29</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eideshelfer 27c—29</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. u</hi>. 30, 1. Hier umfasst der Bezirk, dem die Eideshilfe entstammen soll, nur Ein Hundred, dagegen drei <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 30, 2; letzteres ist also leichter</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See below</hi> 30, 1. Here the district from which the oath-helpers are to be drawn comprises only one hundred, as against three <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 30, 2; the latter is therefore easier</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dm's Zufügung zu Q <hi rend="italic">aut extra</hi> zerstört Cnuts Sinn und entstand wohl, weil Schreiber fälschlich <hi rend="italic">ordalium in hundreto</hi> zusammenzog, wie auch Schmid hier und in Hn keine Interpunktion dazwischen setzt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Dm's addition to Q, <hi rend="italic">aut extra</hi>, destroys Cnut's sense, and probably arose because scribes wrongly took <hi rend="italic">ordalium in hundreto</hi> together, just as Schmid too, here and in Hn, puts no punctuation between them</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘who has never been frequently accused.’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">To complete the A.S. formula <hi rend="italic">him</hi> has to be understood, <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> <hi rend="italic">him naðer ne burste</hi>, etc., cf. I Atr. 1, 2.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann takes this to mean that the compurgators must be found by the accused within the hundred to which he belongs, cf. A, <hi rend="italic">innan his hundrede</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22.robnote.n.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. I Cn. 5, 4.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_22.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>hundrede</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i. his h.</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
